WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:06.819
Let's go to Bethany from Oklahoma. Bethany
from Oklahoma. You're on the air.

00:00:06.819 --> 00:00:18.970
Hi, can you hear me? Yes, I can. Oh, perfect.
I I actually hopped on here not and not even

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:24.939
realizing you were filming, I was just hoping
to catch you. I don't know what time you will

00:00:24.939 --> 00:00:31.230
start the show. So I happen to hop on and
I got called. This is crazy beautiful. I guess

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:38.190
my question is, and in the past few days,
you've been talking about how Biden is being

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:45.559
and being criticized for all of his executive
orders. Yes. And we talked about how he's

00:00:45.559 --> 00:00:52.920
doing what people want him to do. But the
critique I'm seeing from liberal friends is

00:00:52.920 --> 00:01:00.930
that since we control the House and the Senate
now, why isn't he going about it through legislation?

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:06.540
Because he doesn't necessarily have to get
Republicans on board, does he?

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:10.979
So a couple of thoughts, obviously, what you
say. Yeah, this is an important question.

00:01:10.979 --> 00:01:17.280
So there's a few different things, Bethany.
First of all, if the things Joe Biden if Joe

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:23.350
Biden is dealing with actual emergencies via
executive order, then you have to do it as

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:29.230
quickly as possible. And so if if we agree,
some of these things have to be changed right

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:34.799
away. And I agree that some of the things
that that that Biden did via executive order

00:01:34.799 --> 00:01:38.479
do have to be changed right away. You do the
executive order and then you try to get a

00:01:38.479 --> 00:01:43.259
more permanent legislative infrastructure
in the next two years during which Joe Biden

00:01:43.259 --> 00:01:49.470
will have the control of the House and Senate.
So that that argument, the idea that you don't

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:54.060
need to do any executive orders because you
have control and you can do it all, that,

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:57.180
that that's not a good argument, number one,
because if you have an actual emergency, you

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:01.580
need to deal with it as quickly as possible.
Number two, not everything can be done with

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:07.479
a simple majority. There are things that that
require 60 votes in the Senate in order to

00:02:07.479 --> 00:02:12.620
get done. And so it's not quite so simple.
Now with something like covid relief, I'm

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:17.379
ready for Biden to stop the meetings with
Republicans. It was fine to do the meeting.

00:02:17.379 --> 00:02:22.120
It was fine to listen to Republicans who want
600 billion instead of one point nine trillion.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:27.530
But you can use budget reconciliation to pass
covid relief with a simple majority and it's

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:32.450
time to do it. So I think that any you know,
any time you hear such a general critique,

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:36.709
Bethanie, like Biden doesn't need to do any
executive orders because he has the House

00:02:36.709 --> 00:02:42.480
and Senate and can just do everything legislatively.
It's such a general assessment that it almost

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:47.530
certainly it falls short as an analysis. And
that's exactly the case. It's much more complicated

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:52.440
than that.
Gotcha. Yeah, that makes sense, and I had

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:57.060
forgotten that part about, you know, of course,
things sometimes require more than a simple

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:01.970
majority that is absolutely accurate.
And it takes time and it takes time. I mean,

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:07.710
even even without Republican obstruction,
a lot of these things do have to go through

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:12.940
committee. And, you know, I'm not defending
the speed at which the covid stuff is being

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:17.750
done. I would have liked to see Biden do the
meeting with Republicans on January 22nd,

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:22.790
and we could already be moving beyond it.
But I understand why he's giving them a meeting

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:29.799
now. It's just time to act and get it done.
Yep, and I like what you said about, you know,

00:03:29.799 --> 00:03:36.470
if it's true that they want to follow up some
of this stuff with legislation that does have

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:43.580
a longer, you know, hold. Yes. That that makes
more sense to and that is what I will come

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:48.159
back with when I hear that talking point.
Yeah. I mean, the critique that in general,

00:03:48.159 --> 00:03:52.349
executive orders are a problem because the
next president can just undo it. That's always

00:03:52.349 --> 00:03:56.890
been a critique. That's that's not that's
not different than something that could be

00:03:56.890 --> 00:04:01.459
said in the past. That doesn't really change
whether for the time being that executive

00:04:01.459 --> 00:04:04.629
orders can be done. Joe Biden is right or
wrong to use them.

00:04:04.629 --> 00:04:09.860
Gotcha.
Well, thank you. Yeah, that's really all I

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:14.349
mainly just listening, but I did have that
question that's been popping in my head while

00:04:14.349 --> 00:04:19.770
I've been watching your show this week.
All right. Thanks, Bethany. Bethany from Oklahoma.

00:04:19.770 --> 00:05:42.880
Great to hear from you and hope to hear from

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:47.660
you again.

